\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Come unto me, ye weary,
\par And I will give you rest!
\par O blessed voice of Jesus,
\par Which comes to hearts oppressed!
\par It tells of benediction,
\par Of pardon, grace, and peace,
\par Of joy that hath no ending,
\par Of love that cannot cease.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Come unto me, ye wandrers,
\par And I will give you light!
\par O loving voice of Jesus,
\par Which comes to cheer the night!
\par Our hearts were filled with sadness,
\par And we had lost our way;
\par But Thou hast brought us gladness,
\par And songs at break of day.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Come unto me, ye fainting,
\par And I will give you life!
\par O quickening voice of Jesus,
\par Which comes to aid our strife!
\par The foe is stern and eager;
\par The fight is fierce and long;
\par But Thou hast made us mighty,
\par And stronger than the strong.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And whosoever cometh
\par I will not cast him out!
\par O welcome voice of Jesus,
\par Which drives away our doubt,
\par Which calls us, very sinners,
\par Unworthy though we be
\par Of love so free and boundless,
\par To come, dear Lord, to Thee.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

